 "history": {
  "generations": [
   {
    "text": "(Verse 1)  \nI was a shepherd boy in a land where the winds blew loud,  \nA dreamer with a crown in his hand, I was born to the proud.  \nThe gods didn’t speak, the stars didn’t guide,  \nI walked the earth with a destiny that I’d have to ride.  \n\n(Chorus)  \nOh, I was the king of the Macedon,  \nA warrior with a heart that was bold.  \nI conquered the world with my sword and my will,  \nA legend that no one could fill.  \n\n(Verse 2)  \nI rode through the deserts, I crossed the seas,  \nA king of the East, a king of the seas.  \nThe Greeks called me a monster, the Romans called me a fool,  \nBut I was the one who made history, I was the one who took hold.  \n\n(Chorus)  \nOh, I was the king of the Macedon,  \nA warrior with a heart that was bold.  \nI conquered the world with my sword and my will,  \nA legend that no one could fill.  \n\n(Verse 3)  \nI built the empire, I carved the names,  \nA king who ruled with a fire that burned.  \nThe world listened, the gods watched, the stars aligned,  \nI was the one who made the world a new kind of man.  \n\n(Chorus)  \nOh, I was the king of the Macedon,  \nA warrior with a heart that was bold.  \nI conquered the world with my sword and my will,  \nA legend that no one could fill.  \n\n(Outro)  \nSo here’s to the king who walked the earth,  \nA man who changed the course of the world.  \nWith a crown on his head, and a heart full of fire,  \nI’ll forever be the king of the Macedon.  \n\nPeace!",
